{
  "$comment": [
    "PLTF-02 deliverable 13 / sub-PRD D3 — the COMMITTED parity manifest.",
    "",
    "PRD §8.10: 'TypeScript and Python SDKs MUST share an OpenAPI-generated core and provide",
    "streaming, wait/cancel, typed errors and webhook verification.' A capability present in one",
    "language only falsifies that sentence, so the two SDKs are held to one file rather than to two",
    "sets of good intentions.",
    "",
    "This package's test/parity.test.ts asserts, in BOTH directions, that `exports` equals the runtime",
    "export set of src/sdk.ts and that `operations` equals the public /v1 operation ids derived from",
    "the generated path map. Adding a public export without adding it here fails the suite; leaving a",
    "name here with no export fails it too. PLTF-03 reads this file READ-ONLY and asserts its own",
    "surface against `capabilities[].python`.",
    "",
    "`operations` is DERIVED, not curated: it is every operation id in",
    "packages/contracts/src/generated/paths.ts whose path does not contain '/internal' (PRD §8.11,",
    "sub-PRD D8). It is committed so that a reviewer can see the surface without running anything, and",
    "so that an operation silently disappearing from the document fails a test.",
    "",
    "If a capability cannot be spelled idiomatically in both languages, the fix is a docs PR amending",
    "sub-PRD D3 and BOTH PLTF-02 and PLTF-03 — never a fork of this file."
  ],
